NAME
       free - show how much memory and swap is used and free

SYNOPSIS
       free [-h] [-m] [-g]

DESCRIPTION
       free prints two lines: Mem (the RAM) and Swap. The columns:

       total        all of it
       used         in use by programs
       free         not used for anything at all
       buff/cache   used by the kernel to cache files; given back when
                    programs need memory
       available    roughly how much programs could still get without
                    swapping: the number to look at

       A low free value is normal on Linux: memory that would otherwise be
       idle is used as cache. Check the Swap line after adding swap space
       (or use swapon --show).

OPTIONS
       -h, --human
              Sizes such as 1.9Gi and 512Mi.

       -m     Sizes in mebibytes.

       -g     Sizes in gibibytes.

EXAMPLES
           free -h

SEE ALSO
       swapon(8), top(1), vmstat(8)
